#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176341 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176033 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e77a14c-9943-5494-ae89-a77c7a1888d0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Residuals From a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf731189-32fe-57a4-bde5-3c54274327ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174305} {:answer/id #uuid "1a6379b8-ece0-5a99-844b-b7f486334f38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174306} {:answer/id #uuid "441aa6e9-1299-567b-858c-691df1df7a1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174307} {:answer/id #uuid "4b4cb6ac-32c3-5dd7-9a8f-634d8cdf9d9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174308} {:answer/id #uuid "621b8204-3932-59dd-b595-a75ccb8e4c23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b4cb6ac-32c3-5dd7-9a8f-634d8cdf9d9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174308} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5802a2f-64ed-5fd4-b9cc-65c0cef24d68" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174304}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dd98bac0-93e8-506d-a8ba-d1595548f912" :question/math-academy-id "q-134267" :question/problem "![](images/a7/a7fb89105bc5a11837ed0f416b2327d88202e8e782fa4c114ac47b3d5d15421c.png)\n\nThe scatter plot for the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above.\n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted datapoint?" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(7,-2).$ So, our actual value is $y=-2.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=7$ has the $y$-coordinate $-4.$ So, our estimated value of is $\\overset{^}{y}=-4.$\n\n![](images/92/92a26b8ab019879dec3208878f6a0604c0616776b09e3f8fa916fcab72df3a73.png)\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =-2-(-4) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524960 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176033 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e77a14c-9943-5494-ae89-a77c7a1888d0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Residuals From a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "155561b0-11da-52be-a290-8bc7fd41e681" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524422} {:answer/id #uuid "56a2ddd1-cadc-5a93-9a25-8dddff01f271" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524532} {:answer/id #uuid "aefdfe8c-fa67-577b-98ee-259e0b602d66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524663} {:answer/id #uuid "e0fe8d85-7874-5929-8753-4945ee9ab9ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524773} {:answer/id #uuid "e2a545ba-ef49-5db8-a0d9-0458f6933545" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524778}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0fe8d85-7874-5929-8753-4945ee9ab9ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524773} :answer-field/id #uuid "48948107-5211-5ac2-9e2d-522c9771683b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524871}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "06429645-5834-5aa5-be8c-7530ab34a0e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-134787" :question/problem "![](images/55/553af60aa28cbdd7565259eacc167187bc9c63a5b30cd78a6c14a3c43603fca2.png)\n\nThe scatter plot for the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above.\n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted datapoint?" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(5,3).$ So, our actual value is $y=3.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=5$ has the $y$-coordinate $5.$ So, our estimated value of is $\\overset{^}{y}=5.$\n\n![](images/c5/c558c80b7056b794534146d3b99f399c3084806758f78bd6eddb39e8c89248e9.png)\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =3-5 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525051 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176033 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e77a14c-9943-5494-ae89-a77c7a1888d0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Residuals From a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "288479be-98bd-57e4-9608-f6f04980af8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524457} {:answer/id #uuid "a92e5308-f602-5b56-8117-08f3a63517ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524653} {:answer/id #uuid "cc7640de-088c-554a-a442-df97fc11d882" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524720} {:answer/id #uuid "e5da0595-ab74-5f54-bd61-a8b4f9a3237a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524785} {:answer/id #uuid "ffffc3bb-9a0e-59c2-9d08-ba493528be35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524841}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "288479be-98bd-57e4-9608-f6f04980af8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524457} :answer-field/id #uuid "c15ed523-3e32-50d6-b2d3-15996b2f731b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524922}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e01898f3-3b5c-52d9-b3b4-b90e7c403824" :question/math-academy-id "q-134799" :question/problem "![](images/ae/ae35183698308f87acb254b7141d025bc55f815c49dea54231c713997c6a22eb.png)\n\nThe scatter plot for the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above.\n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted datapoint?" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(10,4).$ So, our actual value is $y=4.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=10$ has the $y$-coordinate $8.$ So, our estimated value of is $\\overset{^}{y}=8.$\n\n![](images/61/61ed1ba4b285ac0d21410ddde91c3ed3882def52cbc500867aa7184114dd8fd8.png)\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =4-8 \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
